## 4. What is a Framework and a Library?

When you start building things (like an AI Agent later!), you don't write every single line of code from scratch.

- **Writing from scratch:** You could build everything yourself, but it takes forever and is often full of security holes.
- **Libraries & Frameworks:** These are pre-made, battle-tested tools and structures created by developers all over the world.
  - A **Library** is like a toolbox you borrow (e.g., grab a hammer when you need it).
  - A **Framework** is like a fully built house skeleton; it gives you rigid rules and structures to build your application safely and quickly.

> 🔑 **The simplest way to tell them apart:**
> **You call a library** — you decide when to grab the hammer.
> **A framework calls you** — the house skeleton decides where your code goes, and runs it at the right moment.

